# Integrated bootstrap implementation draft

2026-10-09. DRAFT_NONAUTHORITATIVE; implementation remains open.
Design: rq2_h1_bootstrap_integration_design_v1.md. Root is the sole writer.

Current code implements a private bounded global journal and a per-bootstrap
journal inside BootstrapOwner. The declaration fixes the study path, symbolic
manifest pin, training_ub ordinal and logical journal bounds. Episode paths are
derived from the obligation identity, not supplied as arbitrary alternative
controller roots. Only unresolved training_ub slot0 is accepted.

bootstrap persists a local attempt, then a matching global claim. The proposal
hash excludes the eventual claim record/head, preventing a circular identity.
The global claim references the exact local attempt head and prospective roots.
After matching claim readback, the owner verifies source configuration bytes and
the pinned RTS source, loads the RTS data internally, extracts only its static
network, and compares network identity, DC bus and every canonical stage UID.
Configuration/source/implementation are rechecked around this extraction.
The static network has no hourly_points; none is read/copied/hashed by extraction.
This does not claim that the upstream chronological loader avoids its own file
reads or memory allocations. No current N row is loaded through load_pinned_current.

The owner then retains profile_checked and constructs the new192 phase controller
internally from the exact obligation-derived origin. It reconstructs and pins
the still-empty controller's clock/obligation bindings, parent event header,
anchor header and genesis record. Canonical serialization follows each existing
writer: controller metadata has no final LF, while this bootstrap journal has LF.
The local controller is closed and discarded before controller_ready publication
or any external retain callback. No live controller is stored on the owner;
the record explicitly carries live_controller_retained=false. Its _check always
denies execution in this draft. Closing every lease before exposure also blocks
unbound inherited Job methods before they can create a Job directory or child.
controller_ready is persisted only after those bindings and exact empty directory
namespaces are checked. Replay rejects Job or parent/clock/obligation suffixes
before global release registration.
The default method stops at controller_genesis_retained. The private owned and
registered development routes below extend it; paired handoff remains open.
The default method returns no producer permission.

Both journals require externally retained heads on reopen, fixed same-process
and same-thread leases, canonical bounded records and a continuous hash chain.
Within a live handle, header and event file identities are checked and events
are reread before returning. This detects ordinary drift; it is not a hostile
ABA or crash-durability certificate. Unknown writes poison the handle and keep
all bytes. A suffix beyond the external retained head is rejected, not adopted.

An existing attempt cannot automatically call bootstrap again. A failed write
with no artifact can reopen as new only when the exact empty head is established.
Attempt-without-claim remains inspectable but cannot automatically resume.
Profile-load and controller-construction exceptions retain a pre_release_stop
with stage, exception type and unresolved status. A partial controller directory
is preserved. Partial controller namespaces are bounded subsets of the six known
genesis directories; existing metadata is bounded-read and all file/directory
views are rechecked. Unexpected execution suffixes or non-plain nodes are rejected.
A retained profile with controller artifacts but no ready record reopens as
controller_artifacts_uncommitted, recovery_required=true. A recorded construction
stop remains pre_release_unresolved with recovery_required=true. Neither state
conceals existing artifacts or permits retry. Partial metadata is retained for
recovery and does not need to be a completed canonical genesis record.
Failures of profile/ready journal publication are not converted
into a successful stop record: unknown writes retain the external-head mismatch.
Reopening profile_verified or controller_genesis_retained is inspection only;
an existing attempt can never call bootstrap automatically again.
Duplicate episode root creation preserves the existing record. Global branch
capacity is checked before the first attempt; logical caps do not prove physical
allocation, full-study storage, wall time or memory admission.

Every global claim is reconstructed from the pinned symbolic obligation, fixed
manifest path, study/profile and derived episode roots, including claims for
other episodes. Its exact proposal digest, bootstrap header/genesis and first
attempt bytes/head must agree. Cross-referenced files are reread after global
replay. Each unreleased claim reserves two further global records (release and
terminal); a globally released slot reserves one terminal, including when its
execution is indeterminate. A new attempt requires three additional records. Header-derived
genesis is checked on every live journal operation.

RunConfiguration binds canonical upstream/config paths, the frozen source config
pin, declared network identity/DC bus, typed solver specification/replay limits/
short Job budget, and a complete declared canonical stage order. The common
study header includes its serialized fields. bootstrap requires this exact type
and compares every StaticProfile field before writing its attempt. Missing or
mismatched configuration and the previous synthetic-profile example fail here.
Network identity and stage inventory are still declarations at this point.

Profile hashing uses the existing canonical JSON encoder: dc_bus, specification,
limits, Job budget and stage_order are hashed separately. source_config uses the
frozen source pin; implementation uses this unit's implementation_identity;
origin_rule uses the normal_h1_model module bytes; need_rule uses the finite
followup assessment implementation identity. These hashes bind code and inputs;
they do not establish a live owner need, network correspondence or admission.
Before hour1+ claims and mutual attachment, a dedicated need-consumption
identity (or equally strong owner identity) must also bind phase-owner's
_assessment adapter and its prepare/FSM consumption. The current need_rule
field covers finite-followup assessment only. The 300-second Job ceiling is
the inherited short development limit, not a full experiment resource budget.

Pre-source tests use an explicit test-only continuation stop and deny source/
network/controller access. Post-claim tests restore the real continuation and
controller constructor, with a synthetic static inventory and a test-only RTS
